-- ============================================================================
-- DC28 - Earth Modeling PROFESSIONAL (intermediate tier) goes deep.
--
-- Flips (earthmodel, intermediate) onto the DC1 deep path by inserting its
-- ACTIVE academy_course_structures row, generated from the repo manifest
-- src/content/courses/earthmodel/intermediate/manifest.json (emitted by a
-- generator, not hand-typed), and seeding the six module quiz banks plus the
-- final exam. Answer keys live only here and in the table.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons: a well is not a vertical line, minimum curvature,
-- landing the tops, the tie table, the cost of assuming vertical, and the
-- well tie workflow.
--
-- Every numeric item traces to the earthmodel teaching oracle in
-- src/lib/earthmodelTeaching.js (wellTies / zoneControlPoints over the golden
-- three-surface model) and reproduces the live intermediate capstone answer
-- key: W2 TopA TVDSS 1496.6634373420557 m, W1 BaseB residual 5, W2 TopB
-- residual 8.318351595797822, W3 TopA residual 1, worst residual
-- 45.02816332199586 (W2 BaseB), and W2 zone A control point x
-- 1610.8719179395334. tieLab.test.js pins the panel math to the same values.
--
-- Tier positioning: the Associate tier (DC12) owns the container (frame,
-- clamp 0/0/180, zones, the 45e6 m3 anchor) and forward-quotes the worst
-- residual 45.028 with its slogan. Nothing here re-teaches those. This tier
-- owns the mechanism: vertical wells tie by exact integer arithmetic (the
-- ledger identity res(BaseB) - res(TopB) = well zone B - model zone B holds
-- exactly, putting 30 m of pinched zone into the eastern wells' +37/+36);
-- W2's build has RF 1.054786175158099 with 111.87696857341697 m east and
-- 270.09489484713185 m down over 300 m of hole; the vertical assumption
-- FLIPS W2 TopA's sign (+26 against the true -35.75883821136131) and drags
-- the zone A control point 210.87 m back to the wellhead while its MD weight
-- of 120 (against 84.8528137423857 m of true rock) survives.
--
-- Bank standard: measured on the length RANK of the correct option and checked
-- for cyclic key sequences, answer-index skew, within-pool near-duplicates and
-- same-claim option pairs before seeding. Across the 132 questions the correct
-- option is longest in 6 pct and shortest in 8 pct.
--
-- Enrollment grandfathering: enforced_from defaults to now() on first insert;
-- the ON CONFLICT update deliberately leaves enforced_from unchanged on
-- re-seeds.
--
-- Ladder note: an INTERMEDIATE enrollment needs an unrevoked ASSOCIATE
-- certification on the SAME app, so the dry-run probes back-stop an earthmodel
-- associate cert in-transaction, and a P3b check proves the earthmodel
-- Associate tier is left undisturbed at 132 questions.
--
-- New em-tie-explorer panel. NO DDL. Data only.
-- ============================================================================

values ('earthmodel', 'intermediate', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-a-well-is-not-a-vertical-line","title":"A Well Is Not a Vertical Line","lesson_keys":["l01-what-this-tier-adds","l02-the-four-wells","l03-md-tvd-and-tvdss","l04-the-tie-panel-map"]},{"key":"m02-minimum-curvature","title":"Minimum Curvature","lesson_keys":["l01-survey-stations","l02-the-circular-arc","l03-the-hold-section","l04-between-stations","l05-w2-in-numbers"]},{"key":"m03-landing-the-tops","title":"Landing the Tops","lesson_keys":["l01-a-pick-is-a-measured-depth","l02-from-md-to-3d","l03-vertical-wells-are-the-easy-case","l04-sampling-the-surface"]},{"key":"m04-the-tie-table","title":"The Tie Table","lesson_keys":["l01-the-residual","l02-the-twelve-rows","l03-the-worst-residual","l04-the-baseb-ledger","l05-what-a-residual-is-not"]},{"key":"m05-the-cost-of-assuming-vertical","title":"The Cost of Assuming Vertical","lesson_keys":["l01-the-vertical-assumption","l02-two-errors-that-do-not-cancel","l03-the-control-point-moves","l04-the-md-weight"]},{"key":"m06-the-well-tie-workflow","title":"The Well Tie Workflow","lesson_keys":["l01-the-workflow-end-to-end","l02-quality-control","l03-the-capstone-walkthrough","l04-onward-to-expert"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
